WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.930
Agencies can run two free, read-only
assessments of their Microsoft cloud,

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.050
and often drop one because
both cover identity.

3
00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:09.725
They answer different questions.

4
00:00:09.725 --> 00:00:11.750
ScubaGear is CISA's tool.

5
00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.984
It asks a compliance question:

6
00:00:13.984 --> 00:00:18.362
does this Microsoft 365 tenant
meet the federal baselines?

7
00:00:18.362 --> 00:00:22.963
It's the tool the directive names,
and its output is what CISA receives.

8
00:00:22.963 --> 00:00:26.938
Microsoft's Zero Trust Assessment
asks a maturity question:

9
00:00:26.938 --> 00:00:30.675
how close is the environment
to Microsoft's own guidance?

10
00:00:30.675 --> 00:00:34.768
It's a community project
maintained by Microsoft employees,

11
00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:39.025
not an official product, and
it isn't a BOD 25-01 tool.

12
00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:41.137
They overlap mostly on identity.

13
00:00:41.137 --> 00:00:44.521
Only ScubaGear covers
Exchange Online, Teams,

14
00:00:44.521 --> 00:00:49.863
SharePoint and Power Platform, where
22 of the 50 mandatory policies sit.

15
00:00:49.863 --> 00:00:52.559
Drop ScubaGear and mandatory policies go

16
00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:55.487
unassessed and the
required reporting stops.

17
00:00:55.487 --> 00:00:59.599
Drop the other, and devices,
network and data go unmeasured.

18
00:00:59.599 --> 00:01:03.738
Even running both is one vendor's
answer about one vendor's platform.

19
00:01:03.738 --> 00:01:07.462
Neither sees another cloud,
the network or the hypervisors.

20
00:01:07.462 --> 00:01:10.300
And a score is a reading,
not a treatment plan.

21
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:14.633
The CISO decides, before the next
production run: approve both tools,

22
00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:19.651
with pinned versions, and keep their
output inside the authorization boundary,

23
00:01:19.651 --> 00:01:22.388
because it's a map of
where the tenant is weak.

24
00:01:22.388 --> 00:01:27.013
Expect the score to move when a version
changes, even if the tenant didn't.

25
00:01:27.013 --> 00:01:30.860
Next, everything beyond Microsoft 365.
